Subject: arm64: dts: allwinner: associate H616 display mixers with the IOMMU

The VE activates the shared IOMMU with all bypass bits cleared. The DE
must then allocate and import buffers through the same translated DMA
interface. sun8i_mixer_bind selects the first bound mixer as DRM's DMA
device, not the shared planes device.

Associate both mixers with DE port 0. H616 User Manual page 207,
Table 3-8 assigns 0 to DE, 1 to DI, 2 to VE_R and 3 to VE. Both mixers
share the DE planes and the single IOMMU page-table domain.

Without these associations, enabling Cedrus on the RG35XX Pro produced
master-0 read faults at physical display-buffer addresses. This patch
adds no bypass policy, driver change, or device-tree overlay.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616.dtsi
@@ -192,6 +192,7 @@
 					 <&display_clocks CLK_MIXER0>;
 				clock-names = "bus", "mod";
 				resets = <&display_clocks RST_MIXER0>;
+				iommus = <&iommu 0>;
 				allwinner,planes = <&planes>;
 
 				ports {
@@ -216,6 +217,7 @@
 					 <&display_clocks CLK_MIXER1>;
 				clock-names = "bus", "mod";
 				resets = <&display_clocks RST_MIXER1>;
+				iommus = <&iommu 0>;
 				allwinner,planes = <&planes>;
 
 				ports {
